25,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings are concerning. Hardware and depots require outside appraisals that delay our audits by weeks, though they do provide independently verifiable data.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"We have a mismatch in talent. Our software partners are overextended with board seats, while our logistics experts are idle and field crews take months to hire.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our success comes from lean back-office tools. Our write-off involved physical premises and labor, while our exits were quiet financial software.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Our liquidity is tighter than it looks. Follow-on calls for equipment-heavy holdings are double the model, and our credit line doesn't value subscription contracts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Deployment is often stalled. Security reviews for medical or financial data take three times longer, and custom hardware has caused significant controller shortages.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, if our credit line is limited, we must be very careful about adding anything that requires expensive outside appraisals or heavy capital.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, that aligns with my data. If we pick a company needing field crews or supervisors, we'll be waiting months before they can even start.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, the data suggests that lean software is our safest bet for returns, but we must ensure the customers actually stay through price changes.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, exactly. And since subscription contracts aren't great security for our credit line, we need a model that doesn't trigger massive follow-on calls.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, it's a systemic trap. We fund a vision, but the reality is a six-month wait for a security review or a missing chip.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,It seems we are all describing a need for simplicity. We need a candidate that doesn't complicate our audit or drain our reserves.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. A candidate that fits our current adviser bench—specifically those logistics experts—might be tempting, but the hiring lag for crews is a dealbreaker.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"We should prioritize a lean, back-office approach. It's where our actual wins are, regardless of the stories we tell.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I concur. We cannot afford another holding that calls for capital twice as fast as we planned.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shion,,Then we must avoid anything with heavy regulation or custom hardware. The path to the first customer must be unobstructed.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
